---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";

const title = "About Age Calculator – Accuracy, Privacy & Method";
const description = "Learn who builds Age Calculator at agecalculatorkit.com, why it exists, how calendar-accurate results are assured, and our editorial, privacy and update practices.";
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <section class="border-b border-hairline bg-white">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-[1200px] px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-8 sm:py-10">
      <Breadcrumbs items={[{label:"Home", href:"/"}, {label:"About"}]} />
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-[720px] mt-6">
        <h1 class="text-[30px] sm:text-[36px] font-semibold tracking-[-1.2px] leading-none text-ink">About Age Calculator</h1>
        <p class="mt-3 text-[16px] leading-6 text-body">A simple, independent tool that does one thing extremely well: tell you your exact calendar age. Built at <strong class="font-medium text-ink">agecalculatorkit.com</strong> for speed, accuracy and privacy.</p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-mute">Independent site • No account required • <a href="/contact/" class="text-link underline underline-offset-4">hello@agecalculatorkit.com</a> • <!--email_off--><a href="mailto:vipulotari1718@gmail.com" class="text-link underline underline-offset-4">vipulotari1718@gmail.com</a><!--/email_off--></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-[1200px] px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-8 sm:py-10">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-[720px] space-y-6">
      <article class="rounded-[16px] border border-hairline bg-white p-6 sm:p-8">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">What it is</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-body"><strong class="font-medium text-ink">Age Calculator</strong> is a free online utility at <strong class="font-medium text-ink">agecalculatorkit.com</strong> that calculates your exact age in years, months and days from your date of birth and a reference date. It also shows total months, weeks, days, hours, minutes and seconds lived, plus your next birthday countdown, zodiac sign and the weekday you were born. Two companion tools cover related needs: <a href="/birthday-calculator/" class="text-link underline underline-offset-4">Birthday Calculator</a> (focused countdown) and <a href="/date-difference/" class="text-link underline underline-offset-4">Date Difference Calculator</a> (any two dates).</p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-body">Calculator math runs <strong class="font-medium text-ink">locally in your browser</strong>. Recent dates can be remembered in localStorage on your device, and shared URL parameters travel with the URL when opened. We do not keep calculator dates in a server database; see the <a href="/privacy-policy/" class="text-link underline underline-offset-4">privacy policy</a>. There is no login or paywall.</p>

        <h2 class="mt-8 text-lg font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Who builds it</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-body">Age Calculator is an independent web project focused on performance, accessibility and correct date math. We are not a government agency, financial institution or medical provider — we build a focused calculator and document its method transparently so you can verify it. Calculation logic and explanatory content are kept together in the project so changes can be checked against the same documented method. Contact us directly at <!--email_off--><a href="mailto:hello@agecalculatorkit.com" class="text-link underline underline-offset-4">hello@agecalculatorkit.com</a><!--/email_off--> or <!--email_off--><a href="mailto:vipulotari1718@gmail.com" class="text-link underline underline-offset-4">vipulotari1718@gmail.com</a><!--/email_off--> (both listed also on <a href="/contact/" class="text-link underline underline-offset-4">contact</a>).</p>

        <h2 class="mt-8 text-lg font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Why it was created</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-body">Many calculators approximate age by dividing total days by 365 or 365.25. That’s quick but wrong for calendar use: it treats every month as ~30.4 days and every year as the same length. We built this one to be <strong class="font-medium text-ink">calendar-accurate</strong>: real month lengths, correct leap-year handling, February 29 logic and month-end borrowing — while staying extremely simple to use. The method is documented step-by-step on <a href="/how-it-works/" class="text-link underline underline-offset-4">how age is calculated</a> with examples.</p>

        <h2 class="mt-8 text-lg font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">How we ensure accuracy</h2>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5 text-sm leading-6 text-body">
          <li><strong class="font-medium text-ink">Completed years → months → remaining days</strong> using calendar anchors and month-end clamping, so the result never contains negative days.</li>
          <li><strong class="font-medium text-ink">Gregorian leap-year rule:</strong> divisible by 4, not by 100 unless also by 400 (<code class="rounded bg-canvas-soft border border-hairline px-1 py-0.5 font-mono text-xs">year%4===0 &amp;&amp; year%100!==0 || year%400===0</code>)</li>
          <li><strong class="font-medium text-ink">February 29 treated as February 28</strong> in non-leap years for countdown stability</li>
          <li><strong class="font-medium text-ink">UTC midnight math</strong> to avoid timezone/DST drift (elapsed days via <code class="rounded bg-canvas-soft border border-hairline px-1 py-0.5 font-mono text-xs">Date.UTC</code>)</li>
          <li><strong class="font-medium text-ink">Shared utility</strong> <code class="rounded bg-canvas-soft border border-hairline px-1 py-0.5 font-mono text-xs">src/utils/age.ts</code> used by all three calculators — fix once, correct everywhere.</li>
          <li><strong class="font-medium text-ink">Automated regression tests</strong> cover month-end spans, February 29, same-day calculations, reversed date differences and invalid age direction before every verified build.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-body">Still, results depend on dates you enter and are for general information (see <a href="/disclaimer/" class="text-link underline underline-offset-4">disclaimer</a>). For legal or official age thresholds, verify with authoritative records.</p>

        <h2 class="mt-8 text-lg font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Editorial &amp; update process</h2>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5 text-sm leading-6 text-body">
          <li><strong class="font-medium text-ink">Original content:</strong> all explanations, examples and FAQs are written for this site; we don’t scrape or copy.</li>
          <li><strong class="font-medium text-ink">Fact-checking:</strong> formulas are cross-checked with the live code in <code class="rounded bg-canvas-soft border border-hairline px-1 py-0.5 font-mono text-xs">src/utils/age.ts</code> and manual calendar tests.</li>
          <li><strong class="font-medium text-ink">Build verification:</strong> math regression tests and the production build run in CI before verified changes are promoted. Content is updated when the implementation or search intent changes.</li>
          <li><strong class="font-medium text-ink">Corrections:</strong> found an error? Email <!--email_off--><a href="mailto:hello@agecalculatorkit.com" class="text-link underline underline-offset-4">hello@agecalculatorkit.com</a><!--/email_off--> or <!--email_off--><a href="mailto:vipulotari1718@gmail.com" class="text-link underline underline-offset-4">vipulotari1718@gmail.com</a><!--/email_off--> with URL and dates — we prioritize calendar bugs.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="mt-8 text-lg font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Focus on simplicity</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-body">No sign-up, no clutter. Enter two dates, press Calculate Age, see results instantly with large touch targets and summary cards. The reference date defaults to today without hard-coding; shareable URL parameters are optional and are documented in the privacy policy because they travel with the URL. It works with keyboard, mouse and touch.</p>

        <h2 class="mt-8 text-lg font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Focus on accessibility &amp; performance</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-body">Semantic HTML, proper <code class="rounded bg-canvas-soft border border-hairline px-1 py-0.5 font-mono text-xs">&lt;label&gt;</code> and <code class="rounded bg-canvas-soft border border-hairline px-1 py-0.5 font-mono text-xs">fieldset/legend</code>, visible focus rings, keyboard support, good color contrast, logical H1 → H2 hierarchy and reduced-motion respect throughout. The layout is mobile-first, uses responsive grids and keeps primary controls touch-friendly on narrow screens.</p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-body">Static Astro output with Tailwind CSS v4, minimal JavaScript, no backend for calculations, long-cache for <code class="rounded bg-canvas-soft border border-hairline px-1 py-0.5 font-mono text-xs">/_astro/*</code> via <code class="rounded bg-canvas-soft border border-hairline px-1 py-0.5 font-mono text-xs">_headers</code>. The page feels instant even on slower connections, which helps Core Web Vitals (LCP, CLS, INP).</p>

        <h2 class="mt-8 text-lg font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Privacy-conscious &amp; ad-aware</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-body">Dates are processed locally in your browser and saved only as localStorage (<code class="rounded bg-canvas-soft border border-hairline px-1 py-0.5 font-mono text-xs">agecalc:*</code>) or URL params if you share them. We use <strong class="font-medium text-ink">Google Analytics 4 (G-QFP5JZ8LMC)</strong> and Google Fonts — disclosed in the <a href="/privacy-policy/" class="text-link underline underline-offset-4">privacy policy</a> with cookie details and opt-out — and keep <strong class="font-medium text-ink">Google AdSense</strong> behind an explicit build flag. Empty ad placeholders are hidden while advertising is disabled, so the interface stays clean.</p>

        <h2 class="mt-8 text-lg font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Trust &amp; transparency</h2>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5 text-sm leading-6 text-body">
          <li>Real contact: <!--email_off--><a href="mailto:hello@agecalculatorkit.com" class="text-link underline underline-offset-4">hello@agecalculatorkit.com</a><!--/email_off--> &amp; <!--email_off--><a href="mailto:vipulotari1718@gmail.com" class="text-link underline underline-offset-4">vipulotari1718@gmail.com</a><!--/email_off--> on every legal page footer and <a href="/contact/" class="text-link underline underline-offset-4">contact</a>.</li>
          <li>Clear <a href="/privacy-policy/" class="text-link underline underline-offset-4">privacy policy</a>, <a href="/terms/" class="text-link underline underline-offset-4">terms</a> and <a href="/disclaimer/" class="text-link underline underline-offset-4">disclaimer</a> based on actual implementation.</li>
          <li>Open-ish approach: you can inspect calculation logic in DevTools (sources) because it ships as readable client JavaScript.</li>
        </ul>

        <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
          <a href="/" class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full bg-ink px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium text-white hover:bg-black transition">Use the calculator</a>
          <a href="/how-it-works/" class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full border border-hairline bg-white px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium text-ink hover:bg-canvas-soft transition">How it works</a>
          <a href="/faq/" class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full border border-hairline bg-white px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium text-ink hover:bg-canvas-soft transition">Read FAQ</a>
          <a href="/contact/" class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full border border-hairline bg-white px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium text-ink hover:bg-canvas-soft transition">Contact</a>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
